# Architecture boundaries

Source of truth: `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/domain-model.md` (ownership), ADR-0001 / ADR-0003.

## This service MAY

- Validate financial inputs
- Perform financial calculations
- Return structured financial results
- Expose calculation capabilities through an API

## This service MUST NOT casually introduce

- Supabase access or credentials
- Database access or persistence
- User authentication or sessions
- User/farm authorization or farm ownership rules
- Conversation state
- Farm CRUD
- Document ingestion
- Unrelated application-platform responsibilities

The **App Platform** owns user identity, farm identity, authorization, Supabase/RLS, and persistent farm/financial state. This service receives explicitly scoped financial inputs from an authorized upstream caller.

## Target vs current

These boundaries are **commitments**, not a backlog to implement App Platform features here. Absence of s2s auth or typed FinancialInput in the repo today does **not** justify adding database access or user JWT handling.

## On conflict

If a request would add any of the forbidden items into this repo, **stop**. Name the conflict, cite `docs/architecture.md` and the relevant ADR, and do not silently introduce the dependency. Legitimate boundary changes require explicit change-control (see `90-change-control`).
